```
$ jci-audit --help
Rust security and license gate: runs cargo-audit, cargo-deny and cargo-about per pipeline context from one deny.toml. `check` gates PRs on live advisories (cargo-audit), policy (cargo-deny) and license attribution (cargo-about); `release-prep` validates reproducibly against a pinned advisory-db; `sync` derives .cargo/audit.toml and each crate's about.toml from the canonical deny.toml, so the tools cannot disagree about license policy; `prune` detects stale advisory ignores; `init` scaffolds or completes a standard deny.toml. `check --deny-stale-notices` flags a licensing change against your committed third-party notices.

Usage: jci-audit [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  check            PR/dev gate: cargo-deny policy, a live cargo-audit scan, and license policy
  release-prep     Release gate: reproducible, pinned-advisory-db validation
  sync             Derive `.cargo/audit.toml` from the canonical `deny.toml`
  prune            Stale-ignore detector for advisory ignores that no longer fire
  verify           Re-verify a past release against its recorded advisory snapshot
  init             Scaffold a standard `deny.toml` and its derived `.cargo/audit.toml`
  publish-record   Self-contained: sign and upload the release record
  wire-ci          Wire the generated jerus-org/jci-audit orb job(s) into a consumer's `CircleCI` config
  check-ci-wiring  Check that the `CircleCI` config matches `jci-audit.toml`'s `[ci]` wiring spec, without writing
  help             Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -v, --verbose...
          Increase logging verbosity

  -q, --quiet...
          Decrease logging verbosity

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

```
